606	  // Hand-off + invocation (DESIGN §6.6, as amended 2026-08-15): swap to
607	  // task:status:running-agent, then fire the endpoint EXACTLY ONCE — never retried, because a
608	  // retry is only safe when the first call is known to have done nothing, and
609	  // the unanswered case is exactly where nothing can be known. Three outcomes:
610	  //  - fired      → a session exists; the item is the agent's
611	  //  - refused    → a status came back, no session exists and none will (a
612	  //                 token / URL / routine is wrong, which no retry fixes):
613	  //                 converge needs-human naming the cause
614	  //  - unanswered → the session may or may not exist and nothing may guess:
615	  //                 the item STAYS task:status:running-agent with the outcome-unknown comment;
616	  //                 a session that started converges it, one that never did
617	  //                 leaves it silent until the janitor's agent leash (§11)
